latest_plan = "Based on the reflection, here's a step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Extract the core pattern:\n   - Identify the non-zero elements in the input grid.\n   - Determine the smallest rectangle that contains all non-zero elements.\n   - Extract this rectangle as the core pattern.\n\n2. Determine the output grid size:\n   - Calculate the maximum dimension of the input grid.\n   - Set the output size to be the nearest odd number that's at least double the max dimension minus one.\n\n3. Scale the core pattern:\n   - Determine a scaling factor based on the output size and core pattern size.\n   - Expand the core pattern using this scaling factor.\n\n4. Create the initial output grid:\n   - Create a grid of the determined output size, filled with zeros.\n   - Place the scaled core pattern in the center of this grid.\n\n5. Apply symmetry:\n   - Mirror the pattern horizontally and vertically to fill all four quadrants of the output grid.\n   - Ensure perfect symmetry by copying elements across axes of symmetry.\n\n6. Refine the pattern:\n   - Identify areas where the pattern could be extended or connected for better flow.\n   - Fill in gaps or add elements to enhance the overall design, maintaining symmetry.\n\n7. Handle edge cases:\n   - If the input pattern touched any edge, extend the output pattern to touch the corresponding edges.\n   - Ensure that corner cells are always set to 0 (black).\n\n8. Create central void (if necessary):\n   - If the input grid has a low density of non-zero elements, create a small void in the center of the output grid.\n\n9. Final adjustments:\n   - Scan the grid for isolated zeros surrounded by non-zero elements.\n   - Fill these zeros with the most common neighboring value to smooth the pattern.\n\n10. Ensure perfect symmetry:\n    - Do a final pass to guarantee perfect horizontal and vertical symmetry.\n\n11. Convert to ColoredGrid:\n    - Convert the resulting 2D list into a ColoredGrid object.\n\nThis plan takes into account the various aspects we observed in the reflection, including the flexible sizing, the importance of symmetry, the preservation of edge-touching patterns, and the refinement process. It also allows for the variations we see in different examples while following a consistent overall approach."
